Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:29:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy: WarTradeRoutes candidate flag (a timing
 attacker fills its trade slots before its war, gold routes, never to its
 target)

The package block's aggressors netted +2 to +3 gold a turn at T30-T40
against +8 to +13 for the other civs, with as many cities and a 3-unit
army. Caravans were offered from T37-T44 and skipped as "useless" (CP: no
trade units in cities of size 4 or less): 0-1 chosen by T80.

For a timing attacker at peace, planned or in its window (not at war with
a major), under the flag:
- trade units get +400 while trade slots are free, and the size-4 rule
  doesn't apply (CvUnitProductionAI);
- no route to the war target (CvTradeAI::GetAvailableTR);
- gold routes first: food, production and wonder routes only when no gold
  route is open (CvTradeAI::GetPrioritizedTradeRoutes).
The two CvTradeClasses.cpp hooks are one check each, through
CvEconomicAI::IsWarTradeRoutesActive. Off in the bundle. Written 6:29pm ET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj2nf4FeZTEHWjvnhhA
